  "cards": [
    { "dot": "cyan", "title": "The one core", "items": ["Playground, published invoke, every eval case AND channel messages call this SAME runtime.invoke(snapshot, inputs, ctx)", "A sub-agent tool call is a 5th, recursive caller (run_source=subagent, P2 · depth/fan-out capped); published + playground run in api, eval + channel run in the worker", "If they diverged, a drift report would score code the endpoint never runs — runtime/ is a pure library (no FastAPI/HTTP types), imported by api + worker"] },
    { "dot": "rose", "title": "Why a frozen snapshot", "items": ["invoke() reads an immutable VersionSnapshot, never the live agents row — editing an agent changes nothing live", "Re-pointing a published version is eval-gated: can't publish a version whose behavior drifted since its last PASS (409)", "snapshot_hash folds in prompt+params+retrieval_config+kb_index+skills — a stale hash would serve a PASS and bypass the gate"] },
    { "dot": "amber", "title": "Not a linear pipe", "items": ["Guardrails run TWICE: input before any model call, output after the final token", "Retrieval is conditional — pre-model when always_on, else a retriever-as-tool chosen inside the loop", "model ⇄ execute_tools is a bounded agentic loop; MAX_TOOL_CALLS (8) caps cost, ctx.deadline_s (30s) caps latency; the approval gate parks the run via LangGraph interrupt() + Postgres checkpointer (survives restarts)"] },
